# Read by run-milestones.sh (the milestone-supervisor skill). Shell assignments, sourced by bash.
# Host-only values (a PATH prefix for this machine's toolchain) go in the gitignored
# .milestones/config.local, sourced after this file. The driver's header comment documents every key.
#
# This file, config.local, the step list, GATE_SETUP, GATE_ENV, the driver and the MAX_* keys are
# hashed into the gate definition. After changing any of them the owner approves the new definition
# (run-milestones.sh approve N gate-definition) before the next delivery, and evidence accepted under
# the old definition has to be taken again.

# The file whose "## Milestone N" sections are the briefs, and where each milestone's report goes.
MILESTONES_FILE=docs/milestones.md   # fill in: the path of this project's milestones file
REPORT_DIR=docs/reports

# The gate: runs in the sandbox after each milestone, and again over the merge when integrate ships
# it. There is no default, and an empty gate makes every launch, --gate, integrate and mutate refuse.
# Fill in one of the two forms below: GATE as the whole check, or GATE_STEPS as labeled steps.
GATE=""
# Steps run in order, each as its own process sharing the worktree (not a shell, so a step cannot
# export anything to the next one). Entries are kind|name|command[|sandbox-only]; kind is
# integration (real services, stores or a browser), replay (recorded external calls) or static
# (lint, types, drift). The kinds show up in the evidence line, so a milestone that touches a store
# or the browser can be seen to have been exercised. A sandbox-only step is recorded
# "not run: sandbox-only" on the host, and a host gate run that skipped one never delivers: with
# such steps, set INTEGRATE_GATE_WHERE=sandbox.
# GATE_STEPS=(
#   "static|lint|just lint"
#   "replay|engine|just test-engine"
#   "integration|api|just test-api"
#   "integration|both-backends|just test-all-backends|sandbox-only"
# )
# GATE_SETUP="make fixtures"          # runs first as the step `setup`: rebuild derived state from committed recordings
# GATE_ENV="sha256sum data/app.db | cut -c1-12"   # a probe; its first stdout line goes into the gate's evidence line
# GATE_TIMEOUT=30m                    # bound on a whole gate run, sandbox and host; each step gets what is left
# GATE_PORT_RANGE=20000-29999         # where a host gate run's GATE_PORT_1..4 come from, so two runs never collide

# Where integrate and mutate gate: host (a temporary worktree of the merge, seeded from SEED_PATHS)
# or sandbox (a fresh sandbox of the merge commit, removed after). Use sandbox when the checks need
# the sandbox image's toolchain, browser or pixel baselines.
# INTEGRATE_GATE_WHERE=host

# Gitignored inputs the gate needs (an env file, a seeded database, model weights): integrate
# copies them into its temporary worktree. Mirror agent-sandbox's worktree_seed.
# SEED_PATHS=".env data/app.db"

# integrate refuses on any other branch; unset means the current branch.
# INTEGRATION_BRANCH=main

# Milestones that deploy; each needs --deploy, given with the owner's yes.
# DEPLOY_MILESTONES="7"

TIMEOUT=12h   # per-milestone wall clock (12h, 90m, 3600)

# Attempt budgets per milestone, with _<n> overrides (MAX_FAILED_GATES_7=5). Exhausting one refuses
# every further launch, --continue, --gate, integrate and mutate of that milestone and writes
# ESCALATED into STATUS.md; only an owner approval allows one more attempt.
# MAX_FAILED_GATES=3
# MAX_FINISHING_TURNS=3
# MAX_HOURS=24

# Container resources for every milestone (agent-sandbox --memory/--cpus); MEMORY_<n> and CPUS_<n>
# override one milestone. Unset falls back to agent-sandbox's own config. Size from the memory log:
# a milestone running a full test suite or a browser wants more than a docs milestone.
# MEMORY=8g
# CPUS=6
# MEMORY_3=12g   # write the reason next to each override

# The agent's model and effort (claude --model/--effort); MODEL_<n> and EFFORT_<n> override one milestone.
MODEL=opus   # the cap for every milestone agent: Opus at most, never the supervisor's own model; unset means the sandbox account's default
# EFFORT=high
# EFFORT_4=max   # a new subsystem, an external boundary or a deploy runs at full strength

# Lanes: milestones in different lanes may run at the same time. Milestones that share a mutable
# dataset or rewrite the same modules share a lane. Unset means main.
# LANE_5=import

# Independent evaluation before integrate: the supervisor dispatches an evaluator against the
# target and commits .milestones/evaluation-<n>.md, which integrate requires.
# EVALUATE_6=1
# EVALUATE_TARGET_6="make dev"   # a local run command or a deployed URL

# The weakening scan's patterns and globs have cross-framework defaults in the driver; override
# them only when this project's test layout differs. GATE_DEFINITION_GLOBS names the files that
# define what the gate runs: a change to one needs an owner approval, as does a change to any
# repository file a step, GATE_SETUP or GATE_ENV names.
# TEST_WEAKENING_PATTERN=... TEST_ASSERT_PATTERN=... TEST_GLOBS="tests/" SNAPSHOT_GLOBS="__snapshots__/"
# GATE_DEFINITION_GLOBS="justfile package.json pyproject.toml .github/"
